            <ArticleTitle>Severe chest pain due to infectious mononucleosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>149-50, 153-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Infectious mononucleosis complicated by acute myopericarditis was finally diagnosed in a 17-year-old boy who presented with sore throat and severe left-sided chest pain. A mononucleosis spot test and heterophil agglutination test turned strongly positive only on the sixth hospital day. The natural course of infectious mononucleosis complicated by myopericarditis appears to be benign.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
